Hermes Max · Command Center
===========================

This package modifies an existing Hermes Agent installation. It is an
independent community project and is **not** affiliated with, endorsed by, or
supported by Nous Research.

Hermes Agent
------------

Hermes Agent is Copyright (c) 2025 Nous Research and is distributed under the
MIT License. See https://github.com/NousResearch/hermes-agent.

Six files in `overlay/` are **modified copies** of Hermes Agent source files.
They carry Nous Research's copyright, and the MIT permission notice in LICENSE
covers their redistribution here:

    overlay/web/src/App.tsx
    overlay/web/src/components/ChatSidebar.tsx
    overlay/web/src/index.css
    overlay/web/src/pages/ChatPage.tsx
    overlay/web/src/pages/SessionsPage.tsx
    overlay/web/src/themes/presets.ts

Six further Hermes Agent files are **not** shipped in this package. They are
edited a few lines at a time, in place, on the machine where it is installed,
by `Patch-HermesCore.py`:

    agent/i18n.py
    tools/approval.py
    hermes_cli/web_server.py
    web/src/i18n/types.ts
    web/src/i18n/context.tsx
    web/src/main.tsx

That is deliberate. Shipping whole copies of those files would silently
downgrade them whenever the installed Hermes is newer than this package — which
happened twice during development, once demoting a security-relevant dangerous
command detector, and once breaking every other language's build. Every patch
step refuses rather than guesses when it cannot recognise the code it is
editing, and every one of them is idempotent.

Everything else in `overlay/` (62 files), together with the PowerShell scripts,
the Python self-tests and the documentation, was written for this package.

Upstream bug reports
--------------------

Development of this package surfaced several defects in Hermes Agent itself.
Where this package works around one, the reasoning and the upstream code
references are recorded in the source comments of the module concerned, so the
workaround can be removed once upstream changes. See CHANGELOG-vi.md and
`Test-HermesPermissions.py` / `Test-HermesSessionTree.py`, which fail against an
unpatched Hermes and pass against a patched one.
